  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Most of the chemical reactions have energy barrier. A positive catalyst in a chemical reaction increases the rate of reaction by lowering the energy barrier. It does not alter the energy of reactant as well as product.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/babcd365-9d44-47a4-92ea-092db83d7932-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 193px;\" /></p><p>In the above graph, the curve in the presence of catalyst is having less activation energy. The enthalpy change<span style=\"background-color:null;\"> is constant a</span>fter addition of the positive catalyst</p></blockquote>",
